<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Konsolidacni Banka says bond issue sold out.</title>
<headline>Czech Konsolidacni Banka says bond issue sold out.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech state-held Konsolidacni Banka s.p. said on Monday that its issue of seven billion crowns worth of seven-year 10.875 percent coupon bonds was fully subscribed.</p>
<p>The bank, which buys out non-performing debt at Czech companies, said in a statement that the issue was sold at par.</p>
<p>It added that the issue is guaranteed by the state, which carries a Standard &amp; Poor's investment-grade rating of &quot;A&quot;.</p>
<p>The issue was lead managed by Komercni Banka a.s..</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
